    skos:definition "A substance, gaseous material or aerosol which has been introduced into the air (either by human activity or by natural processes) in sufficient concentration to produce a measurable effect on humans, animals, vegetation or materials (monuments, etc.): $\\ce{SO2}$, $\\ce{NO2}$, $\\ce{H2S}$, $\\ce{CO}$, hydrocarbons, etc."@en ;
